Contradiction detector design:

```python
NEG_TOKENS = {"not", "no", "never", "cannot", "neither", "nor", "without", "fails", "fail"}
ANTONYM_PAIRS = [{"past", "future"}, {"before", "after"}, {"increase", "decrease"},
                 {"increases", "decreases"}, {"upper", "lower"}, {"positive", "negative"},
                 {"inside", "outside"}, {"ingoing", "outgoing"}]

def quote_contradiction(evidence_excerpt, abstract):
    """Return a list of material mismatches between the quoted ledger text and the source
    abstract, or [] if none detected. Reproducible token-diff rule:
      * an aligned replace where one side carries one member of an antonym pair and the
        other side carries the other member;
      * an unaligned gap of >=3 tokens containing a negation token on either side
        (a denial present in the source but omitted from the quote, or vice versa).
    Only applied when the quote is >=15 tokens and overlaps the abstract enough to align
    (SequenceMatcher ratio of the best window >= 0.35), so unrelated text cannot trip it.
    """
    q = norm(strip_quotes(LABEL_RE.sub("", (evidence_excerpt or "").strip()))).split()
    a = norm(abstract).split()
    if len(q) < 15 or not a:
        return []
    sm = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, q, a, autojunk=False)
    # best window: overall ratio is dominated by the abstract's extra text; use matching blocks
    blocks = sm.get_matching_blocks()
    matched = sum(b.size for b in blocks)
    if matched / len(q) < 0.35:
        return []
    out = []
    for tag, i1, i2, j1, j2 in sm.get_opcodes():
        qs, as_ = q[i1:i2], a[j1:j2]
        if tag == "replace" and len(qs) >= 1 and len(as_) >= 1:
            for pair in ANTONYM_PAIRS:
                if (pair & set(qs)) and (pair & set(as_)) and (pair & set(qs)) != (pair & set(as_)):
                    out.append({"kind": "antonym_replace",
                                "ledger_span": " ".join(qs)[:120],
                                "source_span": " ".join(as_)[:120]})
        if tag in ("insert", "delete", "replace"):
            for side, name in ((qs, "ledger"), (as_, "source")):
                if len(side) >= 3 and (set(side) & NEG_TOKENS):
                    out.append({"kind": f"negation_{'omitted_by_quote' if name=='source' and tag!='delete' else 'added_or_altered'}",
                                "ledger_span": " ".join(qs)[:120], "source_span": " ".join(as_)[:120]})
                    break
    # dedupe
    seen=set(); uniq=[]
    for d in out:
        k=(d['kind'],d['ledger_span'],d['source_span'])
        if k not in seen: seen.add(k); uniq.append(d)
    return uniq
```

Careful: the negation rule on 'replace' where q has "establish" and a has "obtain" - no neg. The insert "while we do not directly show mass inflation" is an a-side 'insert' (i.e., tokens present in a but not q) of ~8 tokens containing "not" → fires negation_omitted_by_quote. The past/future replace fires antonym_replace. Good.

But careful about the case where the quote is a legitimately elided paraphrase (row 96, but that's grounded so we don't call contradiction... I'd call it for all sources to record; for grounded sources contradiction may still be computed. To avoid noise, only compute contradiction when qc != grounded_in_abstract). I'll compute it when qc in {close_paraphrase, not_found_in_abstract}. 

